From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb_wifi: strip mDNS collision suffix in known-host check

When multiple instances of the same device advertise (e.g. different bands/IPs),
mDNS appends " (2)", " (3)" etc to disambiguate. But adb_wifi_is_known_host()
does exact string match against the stored GUID (which has no suffix), so
"adb-xxx-yyy (2)" != "adb-xxx-yyy" → known-host check fails → auto-connect
skipped even for paired devices. Strip the collision suffix before matching.

Aiden-local patch (mDNS collision suffix handling).
---
--- a/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/client/adb_wifi.cpp
@@ -170,8 +170,18 @@
         return false;
     }
 
+    // mDNS appends " (2)", " (3)" etc when multiple instances advertise the same
+    // base name (collision resolution). Strip the suffix before matching against
+    // the stored GUID, which never has it. E.g. stored "adb-xxx-yyy" should match
+    // discovered "adb-xxx-yyy (2)".
+    std::string host_base = host;
+    size_t suffix_pos = host.find(" (");
+    if (suffix_pos != std::string::npos) {
+        host_base = host.substr(0, suffix_pos);
+    }
+
     for (const auto& host_info : known_hosts.host_infos()) {
-        if (host == host_info.guid()) {
+        if (host_base == host_info.guid()) {
             return true;
         }
     }
